13. Git: create branch `feat/part-XX-<name>`, make meaningful conventional commits (feat:, fix:, test:, docs:, chore:), run `git status` before and after, never force-push. Merge into main only after everything passes.
14. Do not over-engineer. Do not add libraries without a reason. Keep code readable with docstrings/comments where they help a beginner learn.
15. Do not claim completion unless you have actually verified it. If something blocks you, report "PART X BLOCKED" and explain the real blocker.

