DESIGN DIRECTION (make it feel like a real product, not a template)
- Visual language: "intelligent + adventurous". Calm, editorial, spacious. A distinctive color system (e.g., deep ocean/indigo primary, warm sunrise/saffron accent, mint success, coral danger) — define full scales, not just single colors. Avoid default-looking Bootstrap/Material styling.
- Typography: one display font + one text font (self-host or use a permitted font source), a defined type scale, tight heading tracking, comfortable line heights.
- Shape/elevation: consistent radius scale, soft layered shadows, glassmorphism only where it helps (hero, floating panels). Subtle motion (150–250ms), respect prefers-reduced-motion.
- Imagery: do NOT hotlink random copyrighted photos. Use generated gradient/illustration placeholders (SVG patterns, topographic lines, route-line motifs) and a component that accepts an image URL later.
- Signature elements to design now (static/demo for now): AlgorithmReceiptChip, TrustBadge (LIVE/ESTIMATED/CACHED/DEMO with distinct styles + tooltip), ProgressRing (score), StatCard, RouteLine decorative motif.

REQUIREMENTS
1. Design tokens as CSS variables (colors, spacing, radius, shadows, z-index, motion, typography) with LIGHT and DARK themes; theme toggle persisted (system default respected); no flash of wrong theme.
2. Component library in src/components/ui with TypeScript props, a11y (roles, aria, focus rings, keyboard support): Button (variants/sizes/loading), IconButton, Input, Textarea, Select, Combobox shell, Checkbox, Radio, Switch, Slider, Chip/ChipGroup (multi-select — will be used for trip types), Badge, TrustBadge, Card, Avatar, Tabs, Accordion, Modal, Drawer (used for "Why recommended?"), Tooltip, Popover, Toast system, Skeleton, Spinner, ProgressBar, ProgressRing, Stepper (wizard), EmptyState, ErrorState, DataTable, Pagination, Breadcrumbs, StatCard, SectionHeader, AlgorithmReceiptChip, Footer/Navbar pieces. You may use Radix/shadcn-style primitives or headless libs if it saves effort — justify choices in an ADR. Use lucide-react (or similar) for icons and Framer Motion sparingly.
3. Layouts: PublicLayout (navbar+footer), AppLayout (collapsible sidebar + top bar + mobile bottom nav), AdminLayout shell. Responsive breakpoints defined; test at 360px, 768px, 1280px.
4. Routing with React Router: public routes (/, /destinations placeholder, /how-it-works, /dsa-lab placeholder), app routes (/app/dashboard, /app/trips placeholder, /app/profile placeholder), admin (/admin placeholder), 404 page. NO real auth yet — leave an AuthGuard placeholder.
